<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikolai Yevdokimov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1804–1873</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Count Nikolai Yevdokimov was a Russian general who rose from the ranks to command in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>. After the surrender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam-shamil">Imam Shamil</a> in 1859 he directed the final conquest of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, in which Circassian villages were systematically destroyed and their people given the choice of resettlement on the Kuban plain or emigration to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, leading to mass expulsion by 1864.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikolai-yevdokimov.jpg" alt="Nikolai Yevdokimov" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Гравюра Георгия Ивановича Грачёва · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Evdokimov_Nikolay_Ivanovich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
